Enhancement: TOML profiles, hooks, observability, and backup telemetry

Vaultic can now load local TOML profiles with `-P` / `--use-profile`. Profiles
support recursive `use-profiles` inheritance, normal command sections, and
named `[[backup.snapshots]]` jobs, so `vaultic backup` can run configured jobs
without paths. Command-line options override `VAULTIC_*`/`RESTIC_*` environment
variables, which override later and then earlier profiles. `backup --init`
initializes a missing repository before running.

Profile hooks run before, after, on failure, and finally at global, repository,
command, and per-job scope. Hook commands never use a shell implicitly and
receive VAULTIC_* and RUSTIC_* context variables. Hook failures can stop,
warn, or be ignored.

New global controls include `--log-file`, `--log-level`, `--no-progress`,
`--progress-interval`, and `--opentelemetry`. Successful backups can publish
metrics to a Prometheus Pushgateway (`--prometheus`) or any InfluxDB v2+
compatible server (`--influxdb-url`, token, org, bucket). InfluxDB publishing
uses the native v2 line-protocol API; telemetry outages warn but do not fail an
already completed backup.

